                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h2" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">A script from the second half of the seventeenth century.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red, luminous vivid scarlet.</seg>
                        <desc>Fine and careful. In the letter <foreign xml:lang="gez">ጵ</foreign> the hook vowel marker
                           is attached to the left side of the stroke: <locus target="#37rb"/>. Only the second part of the scribe’s name, Māryām, remains in the
                           supplication formula on <locus target="#39vb"/>. The first part was replaced by the name of one of the supplicants,
                           <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15595AsrataMaryam">ʾAśrāta Māryām</persName>.</desc>
                       
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; the names of the patriarch, the metropolitan
                           and the king; a few lines (alternating with black lines) on the incipit page of <ref target="#p2_i1"/> and <ref target="#p2_i3"/>; 
                           one or two initial lines of <ref target="#p2_i4"/> up to <ref target="#p2_i6"/>;
                           sections of <ref target="#p2_i4"/> introduced with the words <foreign xml:lang="gez">ṣalota</foreign> (<locus target="#51va"/>)
                           or <foreign xml:lang="gez">ṣalota ʿǝṭān</foreign> and a few other words (<locus target="#57v #58r"/>); words <foreign xml:lang="gez">salām</foreign> on
                           <locus target="#40ra"/> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ṣalot</foreign> on <locus target="#57vb"/>; elements of punctuation signs and
                           Ethiopic numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                     <additions>
                        <list>
                           <item xml:id="a1">
                              <locus target="#3rv"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText">Prayer to Jesus Christ; it is written in a very poor hand; the part on <locus target="#3r"/> is illegible.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez"><gap reason="illegible" resp="MK"/> ክርስቶስ፡ አምላኪየ፡ ኢይትፌጸም፡ <gap reason="illegible" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a2">
                              <locus from="40rb" to="40va"/>
                              <desc type="MagicFormula"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6858PPsnakes">Short prayer against snakes</title>, recited upon people bitten by a snake (ʾarwe mǝdr). 
                                 It contains the name of the supplicant, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15605Zadengel">Zadǝngǝl</persName>. It is written by an unpractised hand. 
                                 A part of this same prayer is written on <locus target="#76a"/> in a crude hand, likely as a writing exercise. </desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ አብ፡ በል፡ አክዮስ፡ አክዮሳዊ፡ ደል፡ መርግዎን፡ አቅለሚድ፡ መልአኩ፡ ለአርዌ፡ ምርድ፡ አኅዝኩ፡ ቀረጽ፡ በቀረጽ፡ እግዚእ፡ <gap reason="illegible" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           
                           <item xml:id="a3">
                              <locus from="74ra" to="75ra"/>
                              <desc type="Genealogy"><title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6591MonGenealogy">Ṭǝnta lǝdatomu la-manakosāt ‘The Origin of the Monks’</title>; 
                                 the text is written by a well-practised hand similar to <ref target="#h2"/>. The explicit (<locus from="75ra3" to="75ra10"/>), which concerns the monks of <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0232TKMG">Tansǝḥe Kidāna Mǝḥrat</placeName>, was added later in a
                                 crude hand.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">(incipit) ዝውእቱ፡ ጥንተ፡ ልደቶሙ፡ ለመነኮሳት፡ እንጦንዮስ፡ ወለዶ፡ ለመቃርዮስ፡ ወመቃርዮስ፡ ወለዶ፡ ለአባ፡ ጳኵሚስ፡ ወአባ፡ ጳኵሚስ፡ ወለዶ፡ ለዘሚካኤል፡፡ ዘተሰምየ፡ አረጋዌ። <gap reason="illegible" resp="MK"/></q>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">(explicit) ምንኵስና፡ ዘአቡነ፡ ዘሚካኤል፡ ዘተሠምየ፡ አረጋዊ፡ ወለዶ፡ ለአባ፡ ገብረ፡ መን<add place="above">ፈ</add>ስቅዱስ፡ ግብፃዊ፡ ወልዶ፡ ለአቡነ፡ 
                                 ብእሴ፡ እግዚ<add place="above">አ</add>ብሔር፡ ዘተንሥሔ።</q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a4">
                              <locus target="#75va"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText">The beginning of <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5851Prayer">Naʾakkʷǝtaka ʾǝgziʾo wa-nǝsebbǝḥaka</title>; it is written in a very crude hand, the same that wrote <ref target="#a5"/>. 
                                 The Trinitarian formula is written by another crude hand.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/> ነአኵተከ፡ እግዚኦ፡ ወንሴብሐከ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a5">
                              <locus from="75vb" to="76ra"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2168PaterN">Our Father</title>; it is written in a very crude hand, the same that wrote <ref target="#a4"/>.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">አቡነ፡ ዘበሰማያት፡ ይትቀደስ፡ ስምከ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a6">
                              <locus target="#77v"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7086QeneBoSadqan">Bo ṣādqān wǝluda betǝka ʾǝlla mannanu ʿālama wa-ʿǝlla ʾelu
        ʾadbāra (Qǝne possibly of the mawaddǝs-type)</title>; the qǝne-poem is written twice, once in column ‘a’ and once in column ‘b’, in a very crude hand, likely the same that wrote  <ref target="#a4"/> and <ref target="#a5"/>. </desc>
                                 <q xml:lang="gez">ቦ፡ ጻድቃን፡ ውሉድደ፡ ቤትከ፡ <del>ያ</del>እለ፡ መነኑ፡ ዓለምመ፡ ወእለ፡ ኤሉ፡ አድባረ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a7">
                              <locus target="#78r"/>
                              <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6957HassabaHegg">Ḥassāba ḥǝgg</title>; it is written in a well-practised hand similar to <ref target="#h2"/>, 
                                 the ink has faded away, making the text hard to read in some parts.</desc>
                              <q xml:lang="gez">በዘንዜክር፡ ሐሳበ፡ ሕጉ፡ ለእግዚአብሔር፡ እምአዳም፡ እስከ፡ ኖኅ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="a8">
                              <locus target="#78v"/>
                              <desc type="Asmat">An ʾasmāt-prayer, which includes <term key="MagicSymbols" ana="#MagicSymbols">charactêres</term>, hardly legible due to faded ink. It is written in a crude hand.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e1">
                              <locus target="#9va #13ra #15rb #17ra #18rb #24ra #25rb #29vb #31va #33vb #37va #44va #56va #62rb #72rb"/>
                              <desc>Correction written over an erasure, in <ref target="#h2"/>.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e2">
                              <locus target="#8ra #8vb #10va #25va #44va #66va"/>
                              <desc>Erasures marked with thin lines.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e3">
                              <locus target="#66rb"/>
                              <desc>An omitted letter written in the margin, in a secondary hand.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e4">
                              <locus target="#70rb"/>
                              <desc>A name has been erased.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e5">
                              <locus target="#79r"/>
                              <desc>Pen trial.</desc>
                           </item>
                           <item xml:id="e6">
                              <locus target="#4ra #73vb #74r #75rb #76rb #77r #79r"/>
                              <desc>Minor notes, scribbles.</desc> 
                           </item>
                        </list>
                     </additions>
                  </physDesc>
                        <history>
                           <origin>
                              <origPlace>
                                 <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0232TKMG">Tansǝḥe Kidāna Mǝḥrat</placeName>
                              </origPlace>
                              <origDate notBefore="1671" notAfter="1675">Patriarch of Alexandria (liqa
                                 ṗāṗāsāt) <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6906Matthew"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Mātewos</persName>  (in tenure <date notBefore="1660" notAfter="1675"/>), 
                                 Metropolitan (ṗāṗās) <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8870Sinoda"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Sinodā</persName> (in tenure <date notBefore="1671" notAfter="1692"/>) 
                                 and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10375Yohanne"><roleName type="title">King</roleName> Yoḥannǝs I</persName> (r. <date notBefore="1667" notAfter="1682"/>) are
                                 mentioned in the supplication on <locus target="#52ra"/>. 
                                 <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10375Yohanne"><roleName type="title">King</roleName> Yoḥannǝs I</persName> is also mentioned in the supplication on <locus target="#55rb"/> 
                                 and Metropolitan <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS8870Sinoda"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Sinodā</persName> on <locus target="#56ra"/>.</origDate>
                           </origin>
                           <provenance>The name(s) of the original supplicant(s) has been erased throughout the manuscript from the supplication formulas and replaced with the names of 
                              <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15595AsrataMaryam">ʾAśrāta Māryām</persName> (<locus target="#3ra #40rb, #51rb #51va #62rb #62va #65ra"/>),
                              <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15596AsrataTsiyon">ʾAśrāta Ṣǝyon</persName> (<locus target="#39va #62ra #62va #65ra"/>), <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15597TsigeDengel">Ṣǝge Dǝngǝl</persName> 
                              (<locus target="#57vb #61va #64vb #73vb"/>), and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15598Maryamawit">Māryāmāwit</persName> (<locus target="#31ra #39vb #63ra"/>). 
                              Their names were added in a secondary hand not much later than <ref target="#h2"/>, in vivid red.</provenance></history>
